        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5473c262-5ff6-597f-b815-c230c71f036d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: 79 Pall Mall, Pall Mall, London\n- People: Nell Gwyn, King Charles II, Zoe Tapper, Sally Hawkins, Bryan Dick, Richard Eyre\n- Works: Stage Beauty, Twenty Thousand Streets Under the Sky\n- Concepts: Grade II listed buildings, blue plaques\n\nFacts:\n- Nell Gwyn was born on 2 February 1650 and died on 14 November 1687.\n- Nell Gwyn was a long-time mistress of King Charles II of England and Scotland.\n- After retiring from the stage, Nell Gwyn occupied a brick townhouse on the site of what is now 79 Pall Mall, and a blue plaque marks that fact.\n- 79 Pall Mall is a Grade II listed building on Pall Mall in London.\n- Zoe Tapper was born on 26 October 1981.\n- Zoe Tapper is an English actress who first came to prominence for playing Nell Gwynne in Richard Eyre's award-winning 2004 film Stage Beauty.\n- Twenty Thousand Streets Under the Sky stars Sally Hawkins, Zoe Tapper, and Bryan Dick.",
